content:
By all his Family, whom Fear, or Avarice Engages to the Tyrants Interest,

Is for the honest Love he bears his Country,

Forc'd to implore your generous Protection;

Which I more hope for from your native Goodness,

Than the recommendation of this Letter;

Gust. My Lord, you need not doubt your Pow'r with me I' obliterate any Crime against my self,

Or ev'n my Country when repented of;

Tho' you must own the Treachery of Beron's Purpose, under the disguise of Friendship,
